/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:9:The right statement is: **every boundary instrument currently built, including Moh's published skeleton, is one-directional.** `N-CEILING` gives `N <= U`; extra structure below `D_1` adds contact and lowers `N`; the filter `N <= 16` therefore cannot reject a skeleton (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:38-54`; `xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:143-153`). The 418 rows are necessary H2 realization targets, not maps, and “pinned to 4” consumes the H2 floor `N >= 4` (`xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:191-218,334-345`). No ceiling has been proved.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:14:0 <= N|D_1 <= a_1(-lambda_f(delta_1))
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:17:is the range allowed by Moh's skeleton and abstract ultrametric completion. Its lower endpoint is not attained by an actual Keller pair. The review says explicitly that the full Jacobian may constrain the subtree and that Moh does not (`xmodel/n-on-the-tree-review-grok46-20260902.md:137-151`). Integration #16 itself reserves exactly this exception (`xmodel/integration16-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md:109-115`). Thus “as built” is correct; “no boundary argument” is not licensed. Candidate (f) must be stated as a no-go for arguments factoring through Moh (1)–(13) plus the major skeleton, not for arguments using new Jacobian coefficients below `D_1`.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:19:There is also a plain factual error in candidate (c). APPROACHES row 20 was run as a standalone formalism lane on 2026-08-23. The canonical inverse-Jacobian connection has identically zero p-curvature, while Tsuchimoto's non-tautological object starts with a Weyl-algebra endomorphism and is not defined on an arbitrary commutative Keller map (`xmodel/sol-pcurvature.md:3-30,423-426,501-528`). That branch is `KNOWN-HOLLOW/retire`, not “never run.” Finite-field realization remains a different, one-way falsification tool.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:21:My allocation answer is consequently direct. Give `D_1` one bounded, exact pilot. If it does not expose a positive Jacobian deficiency at the first post-`delta_1` levels, stop treating a universal `D <= C(N)` as the primary proof target. Move the proof flagship to the Moh endgame—uniform elimination of finite-depth, unbounded-size skeletons—and run the exact same `D_1` machinery backwards on the counterexample side. Keep a small global-invariant probe, but do not fund five speculative ceiling languages at once. The depth count is finite; the coefficients and sizes are not. That is an elimination/realization problem, not evidence that another scalar ledger is waiting to be found.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:23:## 2. A new exact cross-connection: the `D_1` self-different
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:25:The missing joint `f`/`g` subtree can be reduced to a one-colour subtree before any large computation. Work in Moh's monic gauge, put `t=x^{-1}`, take generic `c_2`, and let `tau_i` be the Puiseux roots of `g-c_2`. Set
