/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:56:The first consequence is already stronger than a change of coordinates on the same free datum. Let `B` be a bottom-major disc of radius `delta_B=delta_1`, and let `tau_i` be a shifted `g-c_2` root following a root `rho_i` in `B`. The shifted roots preserve every contact visible at radius `delta_B`, so
