/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:87:Different bottom branches may have different lower `V` data and different radii; no common `c_B` is assumed. Individual weights may be rational and integrality is required only after complete Puiseux/Galois orbit packets are summed. The safe computational relaxation is therefore a rational knapsack over **all** allowed branch types, permitting even arbitrary repetitions and unused major-root mass. A failure to make an integer `N` in this over-approximation is a kill; a hit is only a candidate until Moh's orbit restrictions (8)–(11) and actual root-tree attachment are imposed.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:89:This directly revises the opening verdict. Moh's major skeleton alone is upper-only, but the full Jacobian condition below `D_1` supplies a matching self-different floor term by term. The supposedly arbitrary finer contact cannot change the weight. The remaining datum is a finite branch-partition problem, not a free joint subtree. That is a concrete answer to `OPEN[UPPER-TO-FLOOR]`, though a cofinal `N >= phi(D)` still requires solving `(SD6)` uniformly.
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:91:This also connects two lanes that the present ranking keeps separate. For a fixed candidate `g`, finding `f` is the linear Hamiltonian equation `[f,g]=1`; the banked kappa class vanishes exactly when a polynomial mate exists (`xmodel/hamiltonian-kappa-gate-20260824.md:49-80`). The kappa module has no universal receiver and remains a bad global ceiling strategy (`xmodel/hamiltonian-kappa-gate-20260824.md:180-198`), but on one typed `D_1` skeleton it is an exact obstruction/certificate engine. Candidate (d) should therefore be lowered as a global flow proposal and reused as the local solver inside candidate (a).
/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.I2h68x/inputs/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.md:93:The first cheap gate is now the exact `(SD6)` partition, followed by the no-log condition in `(SD1)`: every branchwise Laurent expansion of `dx/g_y` must have zero residue before it can be the differential of an algebraic `h_i`. Passing both is not a Keller witness; failing either is an exact rejection in its stated scope. This is the strongest proof attack in this submission.
