/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/max12-912-order3-nu-q8-infinity-primitivity-review-claude-20260825.md:43:**Decisive evidence.** `Z!=0` is not implicit: infinity report section 2 derives `r8` nonconstant from `9*r8'=j/u`, `j!=0`, `u!=0`, hence `S=r8^9` and `Z=S/nu^10` nonzero and nonconstant — exactly the terminal review's section 10 discharge route (i). Unit inventory, each traced to a reviewed parent: `pi0=nu/n0` nonzero (gate `n0` unit, fibre `nu!=0`); `S0=rho0^9` and `S1` units (leaf4 claim 3 gcd certificates over `E`, valid at all eight contacts by `gcd(Q8,Q8')=1`); `Z0=S0/nu^10!=0`; `lambda^3=Z0` so `lambda!=0` and finite (balanced degrees, terminal review section 7); `3*lambda^2!=0` in characteristic zero. Orders: `ord_infinity(pi∘phi)=0` since `pi(q_Q8)=pi0` is a nonzero finite value, so `ord_infinity(theta)=2a` with `a=ord_infinity(a0)`, `a0 in C(x)` (Kummer-fixed). Positivity: `theta(q_Q8)=0` and `phi(infinity)=q_Q8` give `2a>0`; finiteness: `a0 ≡ 0` would force the quotient image into the `w=0` locus, which meets `C_Q8` in finitely many points, contradicting surjectivity. The formal expansion `S-S0=S1*theta+O(theta^2)` pulls back functorially along the completed local map at `infinity`, `S1` is a nonzero constant, and the tail has order `>=4a`, so `ord_infinity(Z-Z0)=2a`, which is (4.2). Cubing: `Z-Z0=(T-lambda)(T^2+lambda*T+lambda^2)` and the cofactor takes the value `3*lambda^2!=0` at `infinity`, so `e_pass=ord_infinity(T-lambda)=2a`, even and `>=2` — the parity of `e_pass` traces to the parity-involution square `theta=a0^2/pi`, not to the Kummer cube; the report keeps `e_pass` and the Kummer order three explicitly distinct. Decisive cross-check: (4.5) gives `deg(h)=3*(e_pass+1)=3*(2a+1)`, which coincides exactly with the normalization-jet review section 7 independently derived necessary condition `deg(h)=3*(2e+1)` with `e=a`. Two independent routes agree.
