/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/sol-avenues3.log:12192:xmodel/grok-thmA-review-20260812.md:11:3. **Thm A Steps 3–4.** \(L_A(A^w)=w A^w A'-w A'A^w=0\) in any ring. Set \(\beta=\mathrm{lc}(C)/\alpha^w\in F^\times\), \(D=C-\beta A^w\). Then \(\deg(A^w)=w\delta\) over an integral domain, leading terms cancel, \(\deg D<w\delta\). \(D=0\Rightarrow c=0\); \(D\neq 0\Rightarrow d\neq w\delta\Rightarrow\deg L_A(D)=\delta+d-1\ge\delta-1\ge 1\). One subtraction is complete: among powers, \(L_A(A^j)=(j-w)A^j A'\) vanishes iff \(j=w\) (or \(A'=0\), excluded). Full kernel is \(F\cdot A^w\) by \((K/A^w)'=0\) in \(F(y)\) and \(\mathrm{Const}(F(y),d/dy)=F\) in char 0.
