/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:7643:+Therefore equality is forced. This is the proposed **THEOREM D1-SELF-DIFFERENT** (elementary derivation here; not yet independently reviewed): every shifted root in a bottom-major disc contributes exactly `c_B`, while DETECTOR-NULL makes every maximal minor disc contribute zero. Consequently
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:7647:+q_B = e V_2(B),
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:7652:+Different bottom branches may have different lower `V` data and different radii; no common `c_B` is assumed. Individual weights may be rational and integrality is required only after complete Puiseux/Galois orbit packets are summed. The safe computational relaxation is therefore a rational knapsack over **all** allowed branch types, permitting even arbitrary repetitions and unused major-root mass. A failure to make an integer `N` in this over-approximation is a kill; a hit is only a candidate until Moh's orbit restrictions (8)–(11) and actual root-tree attachment are imposed.
