/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9194:+The branch-count output also answers the packet's concrete choice: start at D=105, not D=120. D=105 minimizes both coordinate degrees and has a depth-three chain. D=120 has fewer old pin groups but larger degrees and root packets. D=112 and 117 have no old pin-4 group at all.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9198:+### Card 1 — D1-SELF-DIFFERENT and exact-weight filter (`NEW`)
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9206:+**Interpretation of outcomes.** If the proof and controls pass, the coordinator's categorical one-directionality reading is false and the campaign owns a two-sided finite filter. If `(SD3)` fails, identify the first shifted-root contact that can become smaller than its clipped unshifted contact; that is the exact flaw and Card 1 stops. If the formula is correct but all 418 rows retain a packet, it still removes joint-subtree enumeration and hands exact inputs to the Moh endgame. If the full filter empties the 418, that closes those necessary N=4 skeleton targets, not N=4 itself unless coverage of all admissible degrees is separately proved.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9208:+**Stop condition.** Stop promotion on any failure of monicity, root association, branch-type exhaustiveness, or orbit accounting. Stop scaling the DP once exact orbit constraints leave a stable large family with no uniform obstruction; pass those finite packets to coefficient elimination.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9214:+**Mechanism.** Work backwards from the simplest permissive survivor: `(M_2,V_s)=(56,4)` with four `V_2=3` bottom branches, each exact weight one. Construct a Galois-stable shifted-root tree for `g-c_2`; reconstruct branch values of `f` by integrating `dx/g_y`; then solve the global linear mate equation in the finite coefficient box `deg f<=42`, `deg g<=105`. The same computation is adversarial: failure yields a missing Moh-endgame condition; success yields the sharpest counterexample seed.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9218:+**Cheapest discriminator.** Before emitting full coefficients, test whether four copies of the `V_2=3` branch type form legal Puiseux conjugacy orbits and attach inside the 60-root major class. Next run the branchwise residue/no-log gate on `dx/g_y`. Both are rational arithmetic. Only then build the sparse Jacobian linear system.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9222:+**Stop condition.** Stop after the first exact obstruction and generalize it before trying another support. Stop the disproof claim at `FORMAL` if algebraization or global degree is absent. Do not widen to D=108/120 until every D=105 permissive packet is classified.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9234:+**Interpretation of outcomes.** A negative/fractional multiplicity kills the branch-cycle row globally without a boundary-size ceiling. If every virtual character is effective and depends only on scalar RH data, candidate (b) collapses to the known identity and stops. If only some isotypic component constrains the infinity permutation, couple that component—not total `H_1`—to the D1 packet.
