/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9948:+1. **Independent proof and typing audit of D1-SELF-DIFFERENT.** Check the shifted-root association, the clipped self term in `(SD3)`, every monicity/genericity hypothesis, and the claim that the enumerator's full-`V` rows exhaust one arbitrary bottom-major branch at fixed `(M_i,d_i,V_s)`. This is now ahead of every other proof task.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9949:+2. **Exact branch-packet filter.** Replace `U_rob=max U` by the attainable rational set in `(SD6)`, first permissively and then with Moh (8)–(11), Puiseux conjugacy, and all radius alternatives. The bounded first output is the surviving subset of the 418 H2 pin-4 groups in `[101,200]`.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9956:+1. **Realize one complete D1 branch packet, not a skeleton maximum.** A branch-robust group and a rational-knapsack hit are necessary data only. Puiseux conjugacy, attachment, and Moh's remaining conditions must all hold.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9970:+The second implemented `(SD6)` as a deliberately permissive rational knapsack. For each group it collected every enumerated lower-`V` branch type, assigned resource `V_2` and weight
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9973:+w(V) = e V_2 [-lambda_f(delta_1(V))],
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9976:+allowed arbitrary repetitions and unused resource subject only to `sum V_2 <= u`, and asked whether the exact rational sum can equal 4. This drops orbit multiplicities, Moh (8)–(11), and mutual attachment constraints, so it over-approximates actual packets. A hit proves nothing; a no-hit is safe conditional on the branch-type exhaustiveness audit.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9985:+Wall time was 25.5 seconds after a sub-second extraction; memory stayed desk-scale. This is a qualitative change: the first lower-side instrument rejects 38 of the 59 first-window targets even after deliberately enlarging the branch-packet space. It also kills the visually tight D=105 example `M_2=-35`; its single-tower endpoint `360/83` must not be treated as attained, but no multiset of any allowed branch weights for that group sums to 4.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9987:+The strongest proof attack is now: independently review `(SD1)`–`(SD6)`, add a fail-closed exact-weight mode, rerun all 418 targets, and then impose genuine orbit packets on the survivors. If the 21 permissive hits all disappear, the pinned-N=4 realization list closes without a coefficient Gröbner system. If some remain, their exact packets are the only rational D1 configurations the coefficient endgame needs to see.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:9997:+with the permissive packet of four bottom-major discs having `V_2=3`. For each disc,
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10000:+delta_1=23/30,  lambda_g=-1/6,  lambda_f=-1/15,
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10001:+q=eV_2=15,      w=q(-lambda_f)=1;
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10004:+four weights sum to `N=4` and consume `sum V_2=12=u`. This is cleaner than trying to force 4 below an unattained `360/83` endpoint. It is still only a permissive survivor: first require that four copies form complete Puiseux orbits and satisfy Moh (8)–(11). If they do, construct `g`, use `(SD1)` to integrate its branch values, and solve the global kappa/mate equation. If they do not, discard it without solver work and take the next exact packet.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10006:+The branch-count output also answers the packet's concrete choice: start at D=105, not D=120. D=105 minimizes both coordinate degrees and has a depth-three chain. D=120 has fewer old pin groups but larger degrees and root packets. D=112 and 117 have no old pin-4 group at all.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10010:+### Card 1 — D1-SELF-DIFFERENT and exact-weight filter (`NEW`)
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10018:+**Interpretation of outcomes.** If the proof and controls pass, the coordinator's categorical one-directionality reading is false and the campaign owns a two-sided finite filter. If `(SD3)` fails, identify the first shifted-root contact that can become smaller than its clipped unshifted contact; that is the exact flaw and Card 1 stops. If the formula is correct but all 418 rows retain a packet, it still removes joint-subtree enumeration and hands exact inputs to the Moh endgame. If the full filter empties the 418, that closes those necessary N=4 skeleton targets, not N=4 itself unless coverage of all admissible degrees is separately proved.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10020:+**Stop condition.** Stop promotion on any failure of monicity, root association, branch-type exhaustiveness, or orbit accounting. Stop scaling the DP once exact orbit constraints leave a stable large family with no uniform obstruction; pass those finite packets to coefficient elimination.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10026:+**Mechanism.** Work backwards from the simplest permissive survivor: `(M_2,V_s)=(56,4)` with four `V_2=3` bottom branches, each exact weight one. Construct a Galois-stable shifted-root tree for `g-c_2`; reconstruct branch values of `f` by integrating `dx/g_y`; then solve the global linear mate equation in the finite coefficient box `deg f<=42`, `deg g<=105`. The same computation is adversarial: failure yields a missing Moh-endgame condition; success yields the sharpest counterexample seed.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10030:+**Cheapest discriminator.** Before emitting full coefficients, test whether four copies of the `V_2=3` branch type form legal Puiseux conjugacy orbits and attach inside the 60-root major class. Next run the branchwise residue/no-log gate on `dx/g_y`. Both are rational arithmetic. Only then build the sparse Jacobian linear system.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10034:+**Stop condition.** Stop after the first exact obstruction and generalize it before trying another support. Stop the disproof claim at `FORMAL` if algebraization or global degree is absent. Do not widen to D=108/120 until every D=105 permissive packet is classified.
/Users/dc/code/math/jc2/xmodel/ideation-20260902T1608Z-sol56.log:10046:+**Interpretation of outcomes.** A negative/fractional multiplicity kills the branch-cycle row globally without a boundary-size ceiling. If every virtual character is effective and depends only on scalar RH data, candidate (b) collapses to the known identity and stops. If only some isotypic component constrains the infinity permutation, couple that component—not total `H_1`—to the D1 packet.
